2025-10-08 12:27:28,791 [WARNING] Skipped idx=119: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='Supporting sentence: In humans, two isoforms of p73 have been primarily identified: the full-length (TA) and the N-terminally truncated (deltaN). The TA isoform, also known as TAp73, is covalently modified by NEDD8 under physiologic conditions in an Mdm2-dependent manner, which regulates its transactivation function. This modification leads to the cytoplasmic localization of TAp73, thereby inhibiting its ability to activate p53- and p73-responsive promoters. On the other hand, the deltaNp73 isoform, which lacks the N-terminal transactivation domain, has anti-apoptotic properties and can inhibit the pro-apoptotic functions of TAp73 and p53. It's important to note that while these are the well-established isoforms, ongoing research continues to explore additional post-translational modifications and regulatory mechanisms that may further complicate the p73 signaling pathway.'
