2025-10-08 12:27:30,467 [WARNING] Skipped idx=560: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='The p73 gene in humans encodes two main isoforms: TAp73 and DeltaNp73. TAp73 is the transcriptionally active form, while DeltaNp73 is a dominant-negative acting form. These isoforms are differentially expressed in various tissues, including the brain and glial tumors. In normal brain tissues, the expression of p73 is typically low or undetectable. In the context of glial tumors, particularly high-grade gliomas, there is a notable up-regulation of TAp73, which may be associated with the inactivation of the retinoblastoma pathway and the subsequent activation of E2F transcription factors. This differential expression suggests that TAp73 and DeltaNp73 play distinct roles in cellular processes, including apoptosis and cell cycle regulation, and their expression patterns can provide insights into the molecular mechanisms underlying tumor progression.'
